            <ArticleTitle>Antithrombotic therapy for cerebrovascular disease. Prevention and treatment of stroke.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>199-206</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Antithrombotic therapy in prevention and management of stroke is evolving rapidly as new clinical data better define indications. Stroke is a syndrome with several pathophysiologic bases, not one clinical entity. Optimal use of medical and surgical therapy requires definition of the specific mechanism of brain ischemia in the individual patient.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
